WQ-01: give a zero rate at zero concentration for orders below 1

bulkrate() computes the n-th order reaction potential as
c1 * pow(c, order - 1). For 0 < order < 1 and a concentration of exactly
0, pow() returns inf and the product with c1 = 0 is NaN, which then
spreads to every node and link the water reaches. Return a zero
potential when the concentration is not positive. For orders above 1
pow(0, order - 1) is already 0, so their results do not change.

Apply from the root of an EPANET checkout at 83e25bb:
    git apply WQ-01_fix.patch

diff --git a/src/qualreact.c b/src/qualreact.c
index 7ce6234..ff97472 100644
--- a/src/qualreact.c
+++ b/src/qualreact.c
@@ -396,7 +396,8 @@ double bulkrate(Project *pr, double c, double kb, double order)
         // Compute concentration potential
         if (order == 1.0) c = c1;
         else if (order == 2.0) c = c1 * c;
-        else c = c1 * pow(MAX(0.0, c), order - 1.0);
+        else if (c <= 0.0) c = 0.0;   // avoids pow(0, <0) = inf for order < 1
+        else c = c1 * pow(c, order - 1.0);
     }
 
     // Reaction rate = bulk coeff. * potential
